nter or win. The legal framework is a promotional sweepstakes model, not licensed gambling, which is why these platforms are available in many states where traditional online casinos are not. What exactly is a fun prize casino? The term blends three ideas: the no-stakes fun of social gaming, the prize-redemption hook of sweepstakes, and the slot-and-table-game look of a casino. Operators use a dual-currency model — a free-play coin (Tournament Coins, Gold Coins) that you can never cash out, plus a premium sweepstakes coin (Promotional Entries, Sweeps Cash) that you can redeem once you've met the platform's requirements. No purchase is ever required; the free-entry method (an AMOE, such as a postcard mail-in) keeps the promotion legally distinct from gambling. If you want the full mechanics explained, the dual-currency model guide walks through every step. The short version: you earn Sweeps Coins for free, play games, and — once you clear a 1× playthrough and pass identity verification — redeem them for cash or gift cards. Are fun prize casinos legal in my state? That depends heavily on where you live. As of mid-2026, sweepstakes casinos cannot legally operate in at least 14 US states . Montana was the first to pass an explicit statutory ban. Connecticut, New Jersey, Nevada, California, New York, and Michigan have also enacted or enforced bans. New York's SB 5935 was signed into law in December 2025; California's ban wiped out roughly 20% of the entire industry's US revenue. Oklahoma's ban takes effect November 1, 2026. Funrize Casino — one of the most-reviewed platforms in this space — restricts access in CA, CT, DE, ID, IN, LA, MI, MT, NV, NJ, NY, RI, TN, WA, WV, and WY. Florida residents can play, but any prize above $5,000 is void by state law. Before you sign up anywhere, verify your state's current status in the 2026 legal state guide . Which platforms do I cover here? I focus on operators where I can trace an actual redemption path — real payout methods, documented bonus terms, and a verifiable AMOE policy. The platforms reviewed on this site include Funrize, MyPrize.US, LoneStar Casino, Chumba Casino, and Crown Coins. I also flag operators like Riversweeps and BitBetWin, which masked illegal"
