tigrisdieselworks.com,0,"Tigris Diesel Works | 24/7 Mobile Diesel & Truck Repair | Seattle–Tacoma Professional 24/7 mobile diesel and heavy-duty truck repair in Seattle–Tacoma. Diagnostics, Detroit DD15, Cummins X15, PACCAR MX-13, Volvo D13, brakes, electrical, DPF and aftertreatment, roadside repair and preventive maintenance. Tigris Diesel Works | 24/7 Mobile Diesel & Truck Repair | Seattle–Tacoma TS TIGRIS DIESEL WORKS MOBILE DIESEL & HEAVY-DUTY TRUCK REPAIR Services Engine Platforms Truck Brands Capability Contact CALL 24/7 24/7 MOBILE ROAD SERVICE Professional heavy-duty truck repair, wherever the truck is. Tigris Diesel Works provides mobile diesel diagnostics, mechanical repair and roadside support for commercial trucks throughout the Seattle–Tacoma corridor. The service is built around reducing downtime. From engine and aftertreatment faults to electrical problems, air-brake issues and preventive maintenance, the goal is to diagnose the problem correctly, explain what the truck needs, and perform the repair on-site whenever the job can be completed safely in the field. 206-573-0384 TEXT TRUCK LOCATION VIEW ENGINE PLATFORMS Detroit DD15 Cummins X15 PACCAR MX-13 Volvo D13 Electrical Diagnostics Air Brake Systems DPF / Aftertreatment Mobile Service Capability Heavy-Duty Diagnostics Engine faults, no-start conditions, derates, sensor faults, electrical problems and communication issues. Roadside Mechanical Repair Field repair for common truck and trailer failures when the repair can be performed on-site. Brake & Air Systems Brake adjustment, chambers, slack adjusters, air leaks and related commercial brake-system work. Seattle–Tacoma Service Area Seattle, Tacoma, Kent, Auburn, Sumner, Federal Way, Tukwila, Puyallup and surrounding areas. 206-573-0384 Call or text with truck location, year, make, model and problem description. 24/7 Roadside Service When a truck is down, send the location and the symptoms first. Including the truck year, make, model, engine and any dash warnings or fault information helps determine what tools and parts should be brought to the call. CALL FOR SERVICE SEND LOCATION Mobile Heavy-Duty Services The website now explains the actual work in more detail instead of showing short generic labels. Customers can see the types of systems you work on before they call. DGN Computer Diagnostics & Troubleshooting Diagnostic support for warning lights, engine derates, no-start conditions, poor performance, sensor faults and network-related problems. The goal is not just to read a code. Fault information is used together with live data, electrical testing and physical inspection to narrow down the actual cause. ENG Engine Mechanical Repair Field service for heavy-duty engine components and mechanical problems on common North American diesel platforms. Inspection and repair work may include cooling, fuel, air-intake, turbo-related, lubrication and top-end mechanical systems depending on the truck and the failure. ELC Electrical, Starting & Charging Diagnosis of batteries, starting circuits, alternator output, wiring, grounds, connectors, relays, lighting and electrical accessories. Voltage-drop testing and circuit diagnosis are used to separate a wiring problem from a failed component instead of replacing parts without testing. BRK Air Brake & Foundation Brake Systems Brake chambers, slack adjusters, brake adjustment, air leaks, brake shoes and related truck or trailer brake concerns. Brake-system work is approached as a complete system: air supply, mechanical actuation, adjustment, component condition and correct installation all matter. AFT DPF & Aftertreatment Diagnostics Diagnostic support for DPF, regeneration, temperature sensors, pressure sensors and other aftertreatment-related faults. The focus is identifying why the aftertreatment system is not operating correctly before unnecessary components are replaced. PM Preventive Maintenance & Inspection Oil and filter service, lubrication, fluid checks, visual inspections and preventive maintenance for commercial trucks and trailers. Preventive service is also an opportunity to identify air leaks, wiring damage, brake wear, coolant leaks and other problems before they cause downtime. Heavy-Duty Engine Platforms These are real manufacturer engine images from major North American heavy-"
